    "result_text": "Tests green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\n**Addressed (agreed):** `NormalizeOwnerEmail` now parses the domain via `OwnerEmails.domainOf(lowered)` instead of its own inline `substring(indexOf('@') + 1)`. There is now exactly one definition of \"the domain of an email,\" so the new helper is a genuine single source of truth for both extraction (`domainOf`) and classification (`isDisposable`/`isDisposableAdjacent`). Behaviour is unchanged \u2014 the preceding regex guarantees a single `@` and a non-empty domain, so `domainOf` returns the same value the inline code did.\n\n**Left as-is (minor, with reason):** the `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)` checks inside `riskFlag`. The reviewer flagged this as non-blocking and defensible; it's the standard null-safe idiom used across this mapper, and keeping the three spec conditions inline makes the method read as a direct transcription of the spec. Extracting a helper would add indirection for no real clarity gain.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is intact and the suite passes.",
